    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "Intuit's chief executive announced an AI-focused restructuring to co-locate teams in strategic hubs. This initiative involves eliminating roles and cutting thousands of jobs to reshape the corporate landscape. Affected U.S. employees were offered a severance package, while offices in Reno and Woodland Hills are designated for winding down. The move represents a massive 17% job cuts across the workforce, marking a definitive shift in the company's operational footprint and future direction.",
